# Tab Count Badges — Always Visible

**Every tabbed UI in BazarCRM must show a count badge on ALL tabs, not just the active one.**
Users need to know at a glance how many items are in each section without clicking.

## Pattern Requirements

### 1. API counts endpoint (not derived from loaded data)
Every page with tabs must have a dedicated counts route that returns all tab counts in one request.

```
GET /api/leads/sales-counts   → { counts: { pipeline, hold, rejected } }
GET /api/leads/workspace/counts → { counts: { all, hold, routed, rejected } }
```

The endpoint should use lightweight DB queries (`.select("field", { count: "exact", head: true })` or `.select("status")` with client-side grouping) so it's fast.

### 2. Fetch counts on mount, not lazily
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — fetch upfront, show on all tabs
const [tabCounts, setTabCounts] = useState<Record<string, number> | null>(null);

useEffect(() => {
  function fetchCounts() {
    fetch("/api/leads/sales-counts")
      .then(r => r.json())
      .then(d => { if (d.counts) setTabCounts(d.counts); })
      .catch(() => {});
  }
  fetchCounts();
  window.addEventListener("bazaar:refresh-counts", fetchCounts);
  return () => window.removeEventListener("bazaar:refresh-counts", fetchCounts);
}, []);

// ❌ BAD — count only known after clicking the tab
useEffect(() => {
  if (activeTab === "rejected") fetchRejectedLeads();
}, [activeTab]);
```

### 3. Badge on every tab — not just the active one
```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — badge always visible, style differs for active vs inactive
{tab.count > 0 && (
  <span
    className="ml-1.5 inline-flex h-4 min-w-[16px] items-center justify-center rounded-full px-1 text-[10px] font-semibold"
    style={{
      background: activeTab === tab.id
        ? "var(--color-badge-bg)"
        : "color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-badge-bg) 70%, transparent)",
      color: "var(--color-badge-text)",
    }}
  >
    {tab.count}
  </span>
)}

// ❌ BAD — count hidden until tab is clicked
{activeTab === tab.id && !isLoading && (
  <span>{tab.count}</span>
)}
```

### 4. Refresh counts after any action
When a lead action changes the data (claim, reject, route, put on hold, resume), always refresh the counts:

```tsx
// After any successful action:
window.dispatchEvent(new Event("bazaar:refresh-counts"));
```

The sidebar, tab counts, and all pages listen to this event and update immediately.

